{
  "requirement": "For a definition-name mapping, `habeas refactor` MUST rewrite each `{impl}`,\n`{test}`, `{cite}`, `{fixme}`, and `{term}` reference that names an old name,\nin the book and in the sources reference discovery considers. For a path or\nnode mapping, it MUST rewrite each `:impl:` or `:test:` anchor that names an\nold file or node. It MUST change nothing else in those files.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.refactor.reference_rewrite`.\n\n**Name mappings: each role that names an old name is rewritten.**\n- `src/refactor/tests.rs#fn[sources_rewrite_references_to_names_and_anchors_to_paths]` checks Rust comments.\n  - `{impl}` and the `:::{fixme}` fence are rewritten from `rules.check` to `core.check`, and the edit count is 2.\n  - The near-miss `{cite}\\`rules.checker\\`` is left alone, so only exact names are rewritten.\n- The same test checks Markdown.\n  - `{term}` is rewritten.\n  - The `{cite}` inside a code block stays literal.\n  - The declaration's own name (`{req} other`) is untouched.\n- `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_requirement_renames_its_references_and_evidence]` is an end-to-end check.\n  - It asserts that `{impl}` and `{test}` in `src/config.rs` become `core.load`.\n  - It asserts that `{cite}` in `md/notes.md` becomes `core.load`.\n  - It compares a snapshot of every file before and after, and only the expected files differ. This enforces \"change nothing else\".\n- `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_term_rewrites_definition_inputs_and_the_texts_using_it]` covers `{term}` in the book.\n- `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_rename_rewrites_the_hash_of_a_node_whose_doc_comment_names_it]` covers a `///` doc-comment reference.\n\n**Path and node mappings: `:impl:` and `:test:` anchors are rewritten.**\n- Path mapping:\n  - `sources_rewrite_references_to_names_and_anchors_to_paths` rewrites both `:impl: data.txt` and `:test: data.txt#line@abc`.\n  - `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_file_rewrites_anchors_and_paths]` does the same end to end.\n- Node mapping:\n  - `src/refactor/tests.rs#fn[anchors_follow_a_node_mapping_and_leave_other_nodes_alone]` rewrites the anchor naming `src/a.rs#fn[f]`.\n  - The same test leaves `src/a.rs#fn[other]` unchanged.\n\n**Nothing else changes.**\n- Option-like lines that are not directive options are left alone: a body line in a directive, and a line inside a code block.\n- A role inside a Rust string literal is left alone.\n- `:impl:` in a plain `.txt` file is left alone.\n- The edit counts are asserted, and the integration snapshot diff shows no other file changed.\n\n**Scope.** The sources rewritten come from the shared `discovered_files` helper, which is the same enumeration reference discovery uses. A separate test of that scope would only re-test discovery. I found no gap.",
